  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116400",
      "title": "Styling Active Navigation Links",
      "lectureOrder": 272,
      "videoOrder": 260,
      "sourceHash": "f258d40d0129dabba99dedb20f743e1489268de3ee3fd608685e777fcc332e3d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Now, setting up links like this is nice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "but often you also wanna give the user some feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 10.233,
          "en": "regarding which link is currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.1,
          "end": 12.9,
          "en": "Here, for example, it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.9,
          "end": 15.123,
          "en": "if the active user would be highlighted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.02,
          "end": 18.81,
          "en": "And we can highlight a link here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.81,
          "end": 23.7,
          "en": "by giving it the selected class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 27.063,
          "en": "That's a CSS class I prepared in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.11,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "But, of course, hard coding is no option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "because then all the users would be hardcoded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 36.273,
          "en": "So instead, we wanna set it dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 41.37,
          "en": "Now, you could try to bind the selected class dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.37,
          "end": 43.83,
          "en": "and come up with some code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.83,
          "end": 47.52,
          "en": "where you take a look at the URL and whatever,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.52,
          "end": 51.96,
          "en": "but that is actually not something you have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 55.23,
          "en": "Instead, Angular gives you another directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.23,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "which you can add to your elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 61.11,
          "en": "which would be the router link active directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.11,
          "end": 63.81,
          "en": "which allows you to define a CSS class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.81,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "that should be applied to this element, if it is the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 71.583,
          "en": "that led to the currently active route being loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 77.03999999999999,
          "en": "And in my case here, I wanna add the selected CSS class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.03999999999999,
          "end": 80.01,
          "en": "to this anchor element if this anchor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.01,
          "end": 82.263,
          "en": "leads to the currently active route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 87.09,
          "en": "Now, routerLinkActive is a separate directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.09,
          "end": 88.68,
          "en": "which must therefore be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.68,
          "end": 92.43299999999999,
          "en": "to this imports array, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 97.32,
          "en": "And if you do that and saved it, you'll see that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 101.223,
          "en": "again, all these users are marked as active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 103.89,
          "en": "And the reason for that is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.89,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "that currently all users do render exactly the same link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 112.62,
          "en": "that leads to exactly the same route, to/tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.62,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "which is the route that is currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 118.28999999999999,
          "en": "So it makes sense that all these links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 123.29,
          "en": "are marked as being active, but that will get fixed soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 123.63,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "because that isn't the behavior I want anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "Instead, clicking on different users should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "of course, load tasks, but it should load tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 136.023,
          "en": "for the selected user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.92000000000002,
          "end": 139.59,
          "en": "So what we actually might wanna do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.59,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "is incorporate the ID of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 147.03300000000002,
          "en": "for whom we clicked on a link into this path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.9,
          "end": 152.13,
          "en": "And we wanna set up a route that allows us to encode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.13,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "dynamic information into the path, so that we can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 158.43,
          "en": "one route that will load one component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.43,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "That will then still allow us to actually show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 164.85,
          "en": "different data for different users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.85,
          "end": 168.27,
          "en": "Put in other words, we wanna set up a dynamic route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 171.153,
          "en": "and that's what we'll do in the next lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
